5. **The main agent orchestrates and verifies; subagents execute.** Surveys go to read-only `Task` subagents (`subagent_type: explore`); migrations go to `Task` subagents (`subagent_type: explore`) whose writes are limited to their own group's files. Both carry disjoint file ownership and structured returns. The main agent re-runs every check itself (never trusts a self-reported pass), commits once per verified group, retries ≤2, and restores what still fails. Spec: `references/orchestration_spec.md`.
6. **One spec, short cross-references.** The durable output is `metds/codearc.md` — directory responsibilities, placement rules, naming and style conventions, plan-component map, migration record, the do-not-rename list. `AGENTS.md` gets a ≤10-line summary section pointing to it (edit `AGENTS.md` only — `AGENTS.md` is a symlink to it), and `.cursor/rules/code-codearc.mdc` gets an always-on pointer. Never fork the spec's content into multiple files.
